Hi Nick,
It was great meeting you today at the workshop.
You need at least 3 points to build a model in Wallace, this is probably why you are having complications. You also unfortunately cannot skip the partition step- this is how ENMeval gets the testing and training data to build and evaluate the model.

And you are correct that making a second and third point as duplicates of the one you have will have Wallace remove them as duplicates. But I cannot say for certain it would be valid to make approximate points nearby to be able to build a model.

Bethany Johnson

